还有人在工作？

473
00:19:13.970 --> 00:19:15.210
That's very, that's absolutely true.
那是真的，千真万确。

474
00:19:15.210 --> 00:19:19.170
Although bizarrely, we were within a studio complex,
虽然说来古怪，我们当时身处一个制片厂园区内，

475
00:19:19.470 --> 00:19:20.990
a small British TV studio,
一个小型英国电视台的制片厂，

476
00:19:21.170 --> 00:19:22.230
but we were not in the studio.
但我们不在录音棚里面。

477
00:19:22.370 --> 00:19:25.470
We were in an actual office in the studio complex.
我们在制片厂园区内一间真正的办公室里。

478
00:19:25.630 --> 00:19:26.330
And yes, as you say,
而且正如你所说，

479
00:19:26.410 --> 00:19:28.370
there were people sort of who were kind of annoyed
当时有些人差不多是那种被我们制造的噪音搞得挺烦的，

480
00:19:28.370 --> 00:19:29.630
by the noise we were making
他们正试图继续手头的工作。

481
00:19:30.090 --> 00:19:32.190
and were trying to get on with a job of work.
而我们就在那里，你知道的，

482
00:19:32.310 --> 00:19:33.650
And we were there kind of, you know,
跑来跑去，制造噪音，

483
00:19:33.770 --> 00:19:35.010
running around and making noise
跳着滑稽的舞蹈等等。

484
00:19:35.010 --> 00:19:36.490
and doing funny dances and whatever else.
所以是的，那确实非常像一间真正的办公室，

485
00:19:36.630 --> 00:19:38.850
So yeah, so it was definitely very much a real office
并且它具备了那种环境的所有优缺点，

486
00:19:38.850 --> 00:19:43.150
and it had all of the pros and cons of that,
我想是的，它感觉很真实。

487
00:19:43.230 --> 00:19:45.110
I suppose, that it was, it felt real.
而且我们希望它给人一种充满生活气息的感觉。

488
00:19:45.210 --> 00:19:46.970
And we wanted it to feel very lived in.
我们希望它……

489
00:19:47.210 --> 00:19:48.130
And we wanted it to,
我们一直希望我们这个版本的《办公室》

490
00:19:48.230 --> 00:19:49.550
we always wanted our version of The Office
能给人一种纪录片的感觉，

491
00:19:49.550 --> 00:19:50.650
to feel like a documentary
仿佛是拍好之后，

492
00:19:50.650 --> 00:19:51.910
that had sort of been made
然后大家都把它给忘了。

493
00:19:51.910 --> 00:19:53.510
and then everyone forgot about it.
它就像是被搁在BBC某个地方的架子上，

494
00:19:53.590 --> 00:19:54.870
And it was just on a shelf somewhere
放了大概10年之久，

495
00:19:54.870 --> 00:19:56.110
at the BBC for like 10 years
然后有人把它拂去尘土，

496
00:19:56.110 --> 00:19:57.090
and someone dusted it off
说：把这个放到电视上播吧。

497
00:19:57.090 --> 00:19:58.530
and was like, put this on TV.
所以我们希望整个片子都给人一种陈旧疲惫的感觉。

498
00:19:58.770 --> 00:20:00.670
So we wanted the whole thing to feel tired.
办公室应该显得陈旧，

499
00:20:00.790 --> 00:20:01.870
The office should feel tired,
人也是，衣服也是。

500
00:20:01.950 --> 00:20:03.630
the people, the clothes.
人也是，衣服也是。

501
00:20:03.890 --> 00:20:04.990
We always were very excited
我们总是非常兴奋

502
00:20:04.990 --> 00:20:06.870
when the plants that we had on the set
当我们在片场摆放的植物

503
00:20:06.870 --> 00:20:07.950
were slightly dying.
有点快要枯萎的时候。

504
00:20:08.670 --> 00:20:09.670
We liked that idea.
我们很喜欢那种感觉。

505
00:20:09.810 --> 00:20:11.550
It was the British, that British approach.
这就是英国人的那种处事方式。

506
00:20:11.710 --> 00:20:12.630
You know, you reflect the weather
你知道的，你通过制作

507
00:20:12.630 --> 00:20:14.390
by just making shows that are depressing.
令人沮丧的节目来反映天气。

508
00:20:15.470 --> 00:20:17.050
And that was what that office had.
而那间办公室就是那样。

509
00:20:17.210 --> 00:20:19.230
It had a slightly tired feel
它带有一种略显疲惫的感觉

510
00:20:19.230 --> 00:20:20.890
because it had been a real place.
因为它曾经是一个真实的地方。

511
00:20:21.830 --> 00:20:23.190
And it's somehow slightly harder
而且不知为何，想要人为地

512
00:20:23.190 --> 00:20:25.310
to create that artificially
营造出那种感觉会更难一些

513
00:20:25.310 --> 00:20:26.370
when you build a set, you know,
当你搭建布景时，你知道的，

514
00:20:26.430 --> 00:20:27.390
you're always striving for that.
你总是力求达到那种效果。

515
00:20:27.550 --> 00:20:29.530
So it had that nice lived in quality,
所以它有一种很好的生活气息，

516
00:20:29.770 --> 00:20:31.550
but obviously also restrictive to shoot in
但显然在里面拍摄也很受局限

517
00:20:31.550 --> 00:20:32.250
and a little bit difficult
而且有点困难

518
00:20:32.250 --> 00:20:34.750
and, you know, and it's not much elbow room.
而且，你知道的，并没有太多施展拳脚的空间。

519
00:20:34.890 --> 00:20:36.850
And, you know, so it was pros and cons.
而且，你知道的，所以有利也有弊。

520
00:20:36.870 --> 00:20:37.510
Right.
没错。

521
00:20:37.630 --> 00:20:39.270
Our camera guys have talked about that
我们的摄影师也谈过这一点

522
00:20:39.270 --> 00:20:40.690
where we filmed the original,
我们拍摄原版的地方，

523
00:20:40.690 --> 00:20:42.370
you know, set in Culver City
你知道的，设定在卡尔弗城的

524
00:20:42.370 --> 00:20:43.350
was an actual office,
是一个真正的办公室，

525
00:20:43.430 --> 00:20:44.410
so no walls moved
所以墙壁是不能移动的

526
00:20:44.410 --> 00:20:46.330
and you couldn't pop anything out.
你也无法把任何东西移开。

527
00:20:46.510 --> 00:20:48.970
And that really just added to the authenticity.
而这确实增添了真实感。

528
00:20:49.330 --> 00:20:51.270
But that's where you guys met.
但那就是你们相遇的地方。

529
00:20:51.430 --> 00:20:53.310
You guys met for the pilot,
你们是为了试播集而碰面的，

530
00:20:53.470 --> 00:20:54.570
maybe Jenner, the table read.
也许是在珍娜那儿，进行剧本围读。

531
00:20:54.750 --> 00:20:57.950
I remember doing a reading for you guys.
我记得当时为你们进行了一次围读。

532
00:20:58.710 --> 00:20:59.830
Gosh, I mean,
天哪，我的意思是，

533
00:21:00.010 --> 00:21:02.290
and then I remember we ordered some food
然后我记得我们点了一些食物

534
00:21:02.290 --> 00:21:04.950
and had some lunch and juSt...
吃了一些午餐，然后...

535
00:21:04.950 --> 00:21:05.190
Yes.
是的。

536
00:21:05.570 --> 00:21:07.650
But I think you were maybe shooting by then.
但我觉得那时候你们可能已经在拍了。

537
00:21:07.930 --> 00:21:08.470
Were we?
是吗？

538
00:21:08.610 --> 00:21:09.210
I think we were maybe shooting.
我想我们当时可能已经在拍了。

539
00:21:09.470 --> 00:21:10.870
I have a photo from that time
我有一张那时的照片

540
00:21:10.870 --> 00:21:12.930
which feels like you're on the set
感觉就像你们在片场一样

541
00:21:12.930 --> 00:21:14.150
and everybody's kind of...
每个人都有些...

542
00:21:14.770 --> 00:21:16.590
I'm sure you're maybe working.
我敢肯定你当时可能在工作。

543
00:21:16.590 --> 00:21:17.610
And we were up and running
而当我们真正去访问时

544
00:21:17.610 --> 00:21:18.930
by the time we actually visited.
我们已经全面开工了。

545
00:21:19.110 --> 00:21:20.470
I felt like a lot of what we did initially
我觉得我们最初做的事情

546
00:21:20.470 --> 00:21:21.090
was remote.
很多都是远程的。

547
00:21:21.490 --> 00:21:22.730
I know that Greg Daniels
我知道格雷格·丹尼尔斯

548
00:21:22.730 --> 00:21:24.490
came and visited us in England
来英国看望过我们

549
00:21:25.010 --> 00:21:27.270
and we sat with him for a couple of days
我们和他坐在一起呆了几天

550
00:21:27.270 --> 00:21:28.570
and we sort of chewed the fat
我们差不多就是闲聊了一番

551
00:21:28.570 --> 00:21:31.370
and tried to talk about how...
并试图谈论如何……

552
00:21:31.370 --> 00:21:32.570
You know, tried to give him a better insight
你知道，试着让他更深入地了解

553
00:21:32.570 --> 00:21:34.470
into why we had chosen certain things
为什么我们为英国版

554
00:21:34.470 --> 00:21:35.310
for the British version
选择了某些东西

555
00:21:35.310 --> 00:21:38.010
and how they might translate to America
以及它们将如何转换到美国

556
00:21:38.010 --> 00:21:39.730
and what the versions...
以及这些版本……

557
00:21:40.170 --> 00:21:41.810
What the equivalents would be in America.
在美国对应的会是什么。

558
00:21:41.890 --> 00:21:42.650
And it was fascinating to me
这对我来说非常着迷

559
00:21:42.650 --> 00:21:43.450
because there were things
因为有些事情

560
00:21:43.450 --> 00:21:45.090
which we assumed
我们曾以为

561
00:21:45.770 --> 00:21:47.710
would be the same all over the world.
在全世界都是一样的。

562
00:21:47.790 --> 00:21:48.150
For instance,
例如，

563
00:21:48.390 --> 00:21:50.050
the idea of an office...
办公室的概念……

564
00:21:50.050 --> 00:21:51.090
A group of people in an office
办公室里的一群人

565
00:21:51.090 --> 00:21:52.450
going to a pub quiz
去参加酒吧问答比赛

566
00:21:52.870 --> 00:21:54.630
is quite a traditional idea here.
这里这是一个相当传统的想法。

567
00:21:54.630 --> 00:21:57.790
You'd go to a trivia night as a group.
你们会作为一个团队去参加知识问答之夜。

568
00:21:57.950 --> 00:21:59.050
And that, I remember at the time,
而那次，我记得当时，

569
00:21:59.650 --> 00:22:00.130
it felt like Greg,
感觉格雷格……

570
00:22:00.210 --> 00:22:01.610
that wasn't as familiar to Greg,
这对格雷格来说并不是那么熟悉，

571
00:22:01.970 --> 00:22:04.950
the idea of kind of the trivia night
那种知识问答之夜的概念

572
00:22:04.950 --> 00:22:05.670
or the quiz night.
或者竞猜之夜。

573
00:22:05.790 --> 00:22:07.390
And I guess maybe they are more common now,
我想现在可能更常见了，

574
00:22:07.450 --> 00:22:08.770
but I don't know that that was as...
但我不知道是不是那样……

575
00:22:08.770 --> 00:22:09.490
And it's interesting,
有趣的是，

576
00:22:09.590 --> 00:22:10.970
it was when they did a version in France,
当他们在法国制作一个版本时，

577
00:22:11.230 --> 00:22:13.150
it turns out that apparently on Friday night,
事实证明，显然在周五晚上，

578
00:22:14.050 --> 00:22:15.830
at the end of the working day on a Friday,
在周五工作日结束时，

579
00:22:16.010 --> 00:22:18.150
the champagne comes out in an office.
办公室里会拿出香槟。

580
00:22:18.550 --> 00:22:18.910
What?
什么？

581
00:22:19.170 --> 00:22:20.730
You know, where I guess in France,
你知道，我想在法国，

582
00:22:20.950 --> 00:22:22.910
I think champagne is just like water in France.
我觉得香槟在法国就像水一样。

583
00:22:22.910 --> 00:22:23.730
It's just everywhere.
到处都是。

584
00:22:24.630 --> 00:22:25.750
And I just thought it was fun,
我只是觉得这很有趣，

585
00:22:25.890 --> 00:22:26.030
you know,
你知道的，

586
00:22:26.070 --> 00:22:27.750
just these interesting variations.
就是这些有趣的变体。

587
00:22:28.870 --> 00:22:29.290
Yeah.
是啊。

588
00:22:29.490 --> 00:22:31.190
How many different countries
现在有多少个不同的国家

589
00:22:31.710 --> 00:22:33.190
is the office in now?
有办公室这个节目？

590
00:22:33.410 --> 00:22:34.470
There was a French version.
曾有一个法国版。

591
00:22:34.590 --> 00:22:36.170
There was a French-Canadian version.
曾有一个法属加拿大版。

592
00:22:36.790 --> 00:22:39.090
There was an Israeli version.
曾有一个以色列版。

593
00:22:39.790 --> 00:22:41.530
There was, I believe,
据我所知，

594
00:22:42.090 --> 00:22:42.290
a...
一个……

595
00:22:42.290 --> 00:22:43.790
I think there might have been an Indian version.
我想可能还有一个印度版。

596
00:22:44.030 --> 00:22:44.790
Oh my gosh.
哦，天哪。

597
00:22:44.810 --> 00:22:46.890
And I think there's a South American version,
我想还有一个南美版，

598
00:22:46.950 --> 00:22:48.450
but I forget where exactly in South America.
但我忘了具体在南美的哪里。

599
00:22:48.650 --> 00:22:49.910
But it was frustrating
但这很令人沮丧

600
00:22:49.910 --> 00:22:51.330
because they would send us copies of these,
因为他们会把这些的副本寄给我们，

601
00:22:51.430 --> 00:22:51.790
but of course,
但当然了，

602
00:22:51.930 --> 00:22:53.250
none of them had subtitles.
它们全都没有字幕。

603
00:22:53.250 --> 00:22:55.950
So it was just speaking in their local languages
所以大家都是在说各自的方言，

604
00:22:55.950 --> 00:22:57.690
and I have no idea whether it was good or bad.
我根本无从判断到底是好是坏。

605
00:23:00.170 --> 00:23:02.790
It's got to just be so amazing.
这肯定太神奇了。

606
00:23:03.470 --> 00:23:03.950
Stephen,
史蒂芬，

607
00:23:04.090 --> 00:23:05.650
when you take a moment and sit in that,
当你静下心来仔细想想，

608
00:23:05.970 --> 00:23:09.450
that you went and grabbed a pint with this guy
你曾和这家伙一起去喝过一杯，

609
00:23:09.450 --> 00:23:11.090
and all these years later,
而多年后的今天，

610
00:23:11.690 --> 00:23:14.510
this idea that the two of you had is everywhere.
你们俩当年的这个创意已经随处可见了。

611
00:23:14.550 --> 00:23:15.490
It's everywhere.
到处都是。

612
00:23:15.530 --> 00:23:17.550
It's got to be just so...
这感觉一定太……

613
00:23:17.550 --> 00:23:18.730
It's like COVID-19.
就像新冠疫情一样。

614
00:23:19.230 --> 00:23:19.870
Oh no.
噢，不。

615
00:23:23.090 --> 00:23:24.310
Yeah, no, it's...
对，不是，我是说……

616
00:23:24.310 --> 00:23:25.270
No, I know what you mean,
不，我明白你的意思，

617
00:23:25.350 --> 00:23:25.870
but I think...
但我认为……

618
00:23:25.870 --> 00:23:27.550
Yes, but I think also what's exciting about that,
是的，但我觉得这其中同样令人兴奋的是，

619
00:23:27.610 --> 00:23:30.870
and I think particularly when you guys began your version,
而且尤其是当你们开始创作你们的版本时，

620
00:23:31.050 --> 00:23:32.350
was that, you know,
你知道的，

621
00:23:32.470 --> 00:23:34.510
we always were a fan of our show,
我们一直都很喜欢我们自己的节目，

622
00:23:34.650 --> 00:23:37.070
but we could never watch it as an audience watches it
但我们永远无法像普通观众那样去观看它，

623
00:23:37.070 --> 00:23:38.630
because we were too immersed in it.
因为我们陷得太深了。

624
00:23:38.670 --> 00:23:39.270
We were there.
我们就在现场。

625
00:23:39.730 --> 00:23:41.610
We'd written it and we were just too involved
剧本是我们写的，我们参与得实在太深，

626
00:23:41.610 --> 00:23:42.990
and we couldn't get any distance from it.
根本没办法跟它保持距离。

627
00:23:42.990 --> 00:23:44.730
Whereas I remember when they would send
而我记得每当他们寄来

628
00:23:44.730 --> 00:23:46.510
the seasons of your show,
你们节目的季时，

629
00:23:46.610 --> 00:23:47.290
the episodes of your show,
你们节目的单集时，

630
00:23:47.450 --> 00:23:48.870
I could watch it like a fan.
我都可以像个粉丝一样去观看。

631
00:23:48.990 --> 00:23:49.470
It was like,
那感觉就像是，

632
00:23:49.570 --> 00:23:50.250
I was like,
我就觉得，

633
00:23:50.310 --> 00:23:51.990
I'm just enjoying it as a fan
我纯粹是在作为一个粉丝享受它，

634
00:23:51.990 --> 00:23:54.130
and not as a creator in the same way.
而不是以创作者的身份去审视。

635
00:23:54.210 --> 00:23:54.450
You know what I mean?
你知道我的意思吗？

636
00:23:54.450 --> 00:23:55.230
It's very, very pleasurable.
那感觉真的非常非常享受。

637
00:23:55.350 --> 00:23:57.990
It was like you get to design your ideal show
就像是你设计出了自己理想中的节目，

638
00:23:57.990 --> 00:24:00.610
and then go off and have talented people make it
然后让才华横溢的人把它拍出来，

639
00:24:00.610 --> 00:24:01.450
and send it to you.
再寄给你。

640
00:24:01.650 --> 00:24:02.130
You know what I mean?
你知道我的意思吗？

641
00:24:02.170 --> 00:24:03.070
It's like sort of a weird,
这感觉有点奇怪，

642
00:24:03.130 --> 00:24:04.030
like an amazing kind of like,
就像是一种不可思议的，

643
00:24:04.090 --> 00:24:04.810
you won a competition.
就像你赢了一场比赛。

644
00:24:05.310 --> 00:24:06.270
You design a show
你设计了一个节目，

645
00:24:06.270 --> 00:24:07.510
and then talented people make it
然后让才华横溢的人们把它做出来，

646
00:24:07.510 --> 00:24:09.230
for many, many years.
一做就是好多年。

647
00:24:09.650 --> 00:24:11.790
One of my favorite experiences
我最喜欢的经历之一

648
00:24:11.790 --> 00:24:14.290
was after we filmed the pilot,
就是在我们拍完试播集之后，

649
00:24:14.730 --> 00:24:15.650
I was in London
我在伦敦，

650
00:24:15.650 --> 00:24:19.270
and you and Ricky grabbed drinks with me
你和瑞奇找我一起去喝了酒。

651
00:24:19.270 --> 00:24:20.970
at, is it called the Groucho Club?
是，它叫格劳乔俱乐部吗？

652
00:24:21.170 --> 00:24:22.010
That's right, yeah.
没错，是的。

653
00:24:22.270 --> 00:24:22.490
Okay.
好的。

654
00:24:22.730 --> 00:24:24.550
And that was just so exciting.
当时真的让人太兴奋了。

655
00:24:24.730 --> 00:24:27.250
But then I was on the tube
但后来我在地铁上

656
00:24:27.250 --> 00:24:29.370
and I picked up what was like
随手拿了一本

657
00:24:29.370 --> 00:24:31.710
your version of TV Guide
类似于你们的电视指南

658
00:24:31.710 --> 00:24:33.610
and I looked in there
我翻开一看

659
00:24:33.610 --> 00:24:35.150
and there was an article
里面有一篇文章

660
00:24:35.150 --> 00:24:38.510
about how America was going to ruin the office.
讲的是美国版将如何毁了办公室。

661
00:24:40.050 --> 00:24:41.570
And there was a little picture
上面还有一张小照片

662
00:24:41.570 --> 00:24:43.310
of my face in a bubble
把我的脸圈在一个气泡里

663
